            <ArticleTitle>Intraosseous talar pseudotumour: an unusual presentation of gout.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>86-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.foot.2012.12.007</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0958-2592(13)00002-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a rare case of an intraosseous talar pseudotumour associated with hyperuricaemia in a previously asymptomatic patient, treated with curettage and bone autograft. Satisfactory function and pain relief was obtained at 6 months follow up with no evidence of recurrent disease.</AbstractText>
